# The step of Pocklington's criterion (Pocklington 1914; Mathlib
# lucas_primality is the special case F = N - 1): for a prime factor r of
# N and a prime q with N - 1 == q m, if a^(N-1) == 1 (mod N) and
# gcd(a^m - 1, N) == 1 (given by a Bezout witness u (b - 1) == v N + 1,
# b == a^m mod N), then q divides r - 1.
#
# Proof: a^(N-1) == 1 and a^(r-1) == 1 (mod r) (Fermat), so a^g == 1 for
# g = gcd(N - 1, r - 1) (Bezout on the exponents). If q did not divide
# r - 1 it would not divide g, so g | q m gives g | m (Euclid) and
# a^m == 1 (mod r): r divides b - 1 and N, against the witness.
# Moduli: N = 1 + np, r = 2 + rr, q = 2 + qq.

